; lane_proof.run — the COMBINED owner proof on the Dell, ONE session.
;
; Run with:  spike_server.py submit --run-script RAM:LANE-PROOF.RUN
; NOT with --exec: the lane's --exec is not a shell (a redirect inside it
; returns rc=0 and writes nothing), and a single blocked command there wedges
; the agent's whole command path until an owner reboot. Measured, not guessed.
;
; COMMENTS ARE ';'. '#', 'REM' and '/*' are each executed as a command on this
; lane and each prints "object not found".
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; `echo` IS NOT A BUILT-IN ON THIS SHELL. Every marker line printed
; "echo: file is not executable" -- and an unrecognised command is also how
; the first run died, on `Unsetenv`. So this script has no `echo` in it at
; all: progress is read from the two logs, which is where the evidence is
; anyway. A marker that cannot be printed is not a marker.
;
; MIDISEND IS STAGED AS `MIDISEND.V11`, because it is an ABIv11 build, and
; referring to it as `RAM:MIDISEND` gave "object not found" on a run where
; the file was sitting in RAM: the whole M4 and R5 half of the proof was
; skipped by a name.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; THE ENV MUST BE SET HERE, NOT ONLY IN A DOC. My first version of this
; script started MIDISEND and never started RIAPP and never set a variable,
; because the staging document described the env as something "from a shell
; on the Dell". Executed by the agent there IS no such shell, so the run
; would have had nothing to talk to and no MIDI configured -- and the
; symptom would have been a clean, empty, silent log.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;
; ONE SESSION, FOUR QUESTIONS:
;
;   0. BINDING -- which channels will the app answer on, and did any get
;      REFUSED? Read this first: a refusal here means the sound will not
;      come, and listening cannot tell you why.
;   A. M4 INBOUND  -- the Leviasynth on channel 2
;   B. R5 NOTE-IN  -- the 808 on GM 10, the 303 on channel 2, and the
;                     unmapped-note and unbound-channel laws
;   C. R6 OUTBOUND -- melodic output following the Leviasynth channel, and
;                     the clock-out lamp
;   D. COUNTERS    -- NOTEIN seen=/unclaimed=/refused=/dropped=/played=

setenv RIAPP_EVLOG RAM:
setenv RIAPP_LOG RAM:
setenv RIAPP_DEMO 0
setenv RIAPP_MIDI_IN riapp
setenv RIAPP_MIDI_DEVOUT 1
setenv RIAPP_MIDI_CLKOUT 1
setenv RIAPP_MIDI_LATMS 8
; NOTECH IS DELIBERATELY NOT SET -- that is what makes the melodic output
; follow the Leviasynth channel, and setting it would test the other branch.
; It needed an Unsetenv on the first run and that command DOES NOT EXIST on
; this shell: the run ABORTED at that line with "Unsetenv: object not found"
; (141) after 19 ms, so RIAPP never started and no log existed at all.
;
; An unrecognised command stops the script -- which is what this file's header
; warns about for '#', 'REM' and '/*', and which I walked straight into by
; assuming `Unsetenv` rather than measuring it.
;
; A bare `setenv` listing shows RIAPP_MIDI_NOTECH is ALREADY absent, so the
; line was not merely unavailable, it was unnecessary. That listing is also
; what proves the condition the proof needs: NOTECH unset.

; THE LISTENER GOES FIRST AND IN THE BACKGROUND. It listens for 75 seconds,
; so it must be running before the app starts and must outlive both scripts.
; `Run` is asynchronous in AmigaShell; a bare `RAM:MIDISEND.V11 ...` prefix would
; BLOCK and the two scripts below would never be reached.
Run >NIL: RAM:MIDISEND.V11 riapp LISTEN 75 RAM:R6LISTEN.LOG
Wait 1
Run >NIL: RAM:RIAPP.M4
Wait 6

RAM:MIDISEND.V11 riapp RAM:M4-LEVI.MID.TXT
Wait 3

RAM:MIDISEND.V11 riapp RAM:R5-NOTEIN.MID.TXT
Wait 3

Wait 8

type RAM:RIAPP-EV.LOG
type RAM:RIAPP.LOG
